# Pav Law / Gilbert Guide — always align to branding

Before changing **any** Gilbert Guide surface (KPIs, Data, Recommendations, Predictions, Results, Guide/picker, charts, tables, callouts, tabs):

1. **Read first**
   - [`BRANDING-LAYOUT.md`](gilded-goose/clients/pav-law/project-picker/BRANDING-LAYOUT.md) — tokens, typography, chrome, section heads
   - [`REPORTING-BRAND-GUIDE.md`](gilded-goose/clients/pav-law/project-picker/REPORTING-BRAND-GUIDE.md) — color meanings, semantic states, callouts, tables, chart rules

2. **Source of truth** is live Guide tokens in `index.html` `:root` plus those two docs. Do not invent a parallel palette, card system, or recommendation layout.

3. **Hard locks**
   - **No teal/cyan** on Guide surfaces
   - **Gold** only for critical CTA / Solutions ornate callout / rare milestone — never ranks, scores, ordinary badges, or chart categories
   - Ranks / project scores = royal purple (`--gg-royal` / `--gg-royal-mid`)
   - Red / yellow / green = semantic only (negative / watch / positive) and always paired with a written status label
   - Section heads = solid royal-deep + white uppercase title + lavender hint + burnt left rule
   - Recommendation **Do** / Solutions blocks use aged-brass **double** outline + thin royal inner line (`.kpi-related-projects`) — **no diamond ornaments**
   - KPI / goal tiles in the same grid row share equal card height (`.kpi-tile-with-projects` subgrid) on Guide and Metrics
   - Charts use `chartBlock()` with a **required** header title (`title` / `.kpi-chart-head`); newest month first; one color = one meaning

4. **When branding and a one-off design conflict**, branding wins. Update the brand docs in the same change if a new meaning is truly required.

5. **Cursor canvases** (`.canvas.tsx`) follow [`pav-reporting-color-standard.mdc`](pav-reporting-color-standard.mdc) theme tokens. Guide HTML/JS/CSS follows the two branding docs above — do not mix the two systems.

Related: [`pav-law-kpi-charts.mdc`](pav-law-kpi-charts.mdc) · [`pav-law-value-icons.mdc`](pav-law-value-icons.mdc)
